# USDA FoodData Central API key (https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html)
# Used server-side for generic food search.
# Open Food Facts (barcode / packaged food) needs no key.
USDA_FDC_API_KEY=

# Supabase — OPTIONAL cloud sync (v0.2.0). Leave blank to keep the app fully
# local-first with no login. Both must be set to enable the cloud-sync UI.
# These are public values: the anon key is safe in the frontend WITH Row Level
# Security enabled (see scripts/supabase-schema.sql). Never put a service-role
# key here or anywhere in client code.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google sign-in (optional) — enable the Google provider in Supabase, then add
# these to Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs.
# The app uses `${window.location.origin}/settings`, so allow-list:
#   https://<your-production-domain>/settings
#   https://*.vercel.app/settings        (covers Vercel preview deploys)
#   http://localhost:3000/settings       (local dev)
# In Google Cloud Console the OAuth client's Authorized redirect URI is the
# Supabase callback shown on the provider page:
#   https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
